    "controller_support": "full",
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enter the life of Joe and make decisions that affect the story in this turn-based RPG which will have you pondering your own morality. You are thrown into a conspiracy involving the Necronomicon and murderous intentions with Satanic hopes. Get lost in the craziness and do your best to be good, or don't.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Features:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Turn-Based Combat - Challenge yourself with quick combat in an active time battle system which will keep you on your toes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Saving - Save your progress and return later.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No Grinding - All enemies are challenging and capable of killing you. You will not fight the same enemy a thousand times.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Item Management - You are limited in what you can hold and must store the excess.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Voice Acting - Nearly every line is voice acted and will draw you into the world.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Make and Receive Phone Calls - Call mom or wait for the telemarketers.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Compelling Story - Play as the bad guy and pick up the pieces of a troubled life. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Multiple Choices - Choose how you respond in most dialogue events. These choices will affect outcomes in the Gameworld. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Barter System - Trade items (not just cash) for what you want.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Multiple Endings - Play it again and figure out how not to be evil. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Good Length - At 3 to 5 hours, Human Sacrifice has good replay-ability without overstaying its welcome. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Mini-Games - Multiple arcades and field abilities make playing more fun.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Can you be good when you were programmed to be evil?</i></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enter the life of Joe and make decisions that affect the story in this turn-based RPG which will have you pondering your own morality. You are thrown into a conspiracy involving the Necronomicon and murderous intentions with Satanic hopes. Get lost in the craziness and do your best to be good, or don't.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Features:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Turn-Based Combat - Challenge yourself with quick combat in an active time battle system which will keep you on your toes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Saving - Save your progress and return later.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No Grinding - All enemies are challenging and capable of killing you. You will not fight the same enemy a thousand times.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Item Management - You are limited in what you can hold and must store the excess.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Voice Acting - Nearly every line is voice acted and will draw you into the world.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Make and Receive Phone Calls - Call mom or wait for the telemarketers.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Compelling Story - Play as the bad guy and pick up the pieces of a troubled life. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Multiple Choices - Choose how you respond in most dialogue events. These choices will affect outcomes in the Gameworld. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > Barter System - Trade items (not just cash) for what you want.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Multiple Endings - Play it again and figure out how not to be evil. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Good Length - At 3 to 5 hours, Human Sacrifice has good replay-ability without overstaying its welcome. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Mini-Games - Multiple arcades and field abilities make playing more fun.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" 